  },
  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "The final deal keeps S1 strict (24h for all incidents, 48h customer notice) and S4 at 36 months built-in suppression, within Halcyon's red line. S2 sets a 7% failure cap (above the 5% safe limit) with numeric per-model results to customers/regulators but no public publication, and S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 2 years and retrofit to 6 years. S5 makes recall mandatory above 8/100k with regulator-defined scope, but safety notices are only 'promptly'."
 },
